<tr><td align=3D"left" class=3D"text" style=3D"background:#FFFFFF;font-size=
:0px;padding:0 16px;word-break:break-word;"><div style=3D"font-family:Georg=
ia, serif;font-size:16px;font-weight:400;line-height:22px;text-align:left;c=
olor:#121212;">
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">The world=E2=80=99s largest cryptocurrency=
 exchange endured the world=E2=80=99s largest online theft late last week. =
Binance was hit by a $6.3bn heist that, according to experts, was likely th=
e work of North Korean hackers.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">More than $2.5bn of the $6.3bn was taken i=
n one transaction alone. A Binance engineer=E2=80=99s laptop was infiltrate=
d, which in turn allowed the attackers to drain wallets. Binance later adde=
d that there were =E2=80=9Cadditional points of breach=E2=80=9D in its syst=
ems. The exchange said on X it would =E2=80=9Ccover all losses=E2=80=9D and=
 that =E2=80=9Cuser funds are safe=E2=80=9D. It also said it had frozen abo=
ut half the funds targeted in the hack, stopping the thieves from making of=
f with that tranche of cryptocurrency.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Most customers won=E2=80=99t have legal pr=
otections. Crypto users are not covered by formal deposit protections in co=
untries such as the US, UK or Australia, meaning they won=E2=80=99t be reim=
bursed by their governments for their losses if an exchange is hacked or go=
es bankrupt. In Australia, you can claim a capital loss on your tax return =
if you can offer proof that a crypto asset was lost or stolen.</p>
</div></td></tr>
<tr><td align=3D"center" style=3D"background:#FFFFFF;font-size:0px;padding:=
