<tr><td align=3D"left" class=3D"text" style=3D"background:#FFFFFF;font-size=
:0px;padding:0 16px;word-break:break-word;"><div style=3D"font-family:Georg=
ia, serif;font-size:16px;font-weight:400;line-height:22px;text-align:left;c=
olor:#121212;">
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">As Binance worked to contain the technical=
 damage from the hack, it faced fallout from angry, scared users. The compa=
ny announced Sunday afternoon that it had processed $4.6bn in withdrawals a=
nd $1bn in deposits, resulting in a net outflow of about $3.6bn =E2=80=93 r=
epresenting 2.1% of its $171bn in total assets under management.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Yesterday, former Binance CEO Changpeng Zh=
ao warned that crypto scammers are now in =E2=80=9Coverdrive=E2=80=9D, circ=
ulating screenshots of fake recompense schemes that promise $150 in free co=
mpensation for withdrawal suspensions. Binance has confirmed that it is fal=
se information and the screenshots are digitally altered. The hack has also=
 spooked traditional financial markets, with investors also pulling out fun=
ds from Bitcoin exchange-traded funds in the US.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Yi He, co-founder of Binance and longtime =
partner of Zhao, has said that the company=E2=80=99s top priority was to =
=E2=80=9Censure the environment is secure, after which users can withdraw t=
heir funds and Binance can resume operations=E2=80=9D. Alongside a proof of=
 its reserves, the company tweeted: =E2=80=9COur commitment is unchanged: B=
inance will absorb the financial impact of the stolen funds, not our users.=
=E2=80=9D</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">The name Binance was already associated wi=
th crime before the hack. Zhao pleaded guilty to violating US anti-money la=
undering laws in 2023 and stepped down as CEO. It=E2=80=99s no FTX, but the=
 company faces an uphill battle to save its brand from $6.3bn worth of perm=
anent damage.</p>
</div></td></tr>
